      "side": 1,
      "message": "This locking mechanism only works on POSIX systems. On Windows, `fcntl` will be `None`, and the code will proceed without a lock. This creates a race condition where multiple concurrent subprocesses or threads finishing at the same time might overwrite each other\u0027s trace data or corrupt the JSON file. \n\nConsider using a more portable locking library or, more ideally, switching to the \u0027JSON Lines\u0027 format (one JSON object per line) which allows for simple atomic appends without needing to read/rewrite the entire file.\n\n---\n\nIf it\u0027s difficult or too complex, document instead that it\u0027s only for linux.",
